+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static coffee-shop homepage. No build step or runtime dependencies are required.
+
+## WebMCP
+
+`webmcp.js` registers these browser-side tools when WebMCP is available:
+
+| Tool | Arguments | Result / action |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_favorites` | `{}` | Coffee IDs, names, descriptions, detail paths, and navigation IDs from the page. |
+| `list_destinations` | `{}` | IDs, labels, and paths of supported navigation links. |
+| `navigate_to` | `{"destination":"cold-brew"}` | Follows the selected existing link on the same origin. |
+
+The integration follows the [WebMCP imperative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api), using `document.modelContext.registerTool` and retaining a `navigator.modelContext` fallback for older previews. Use a WebMCP-capable browser in a secure context (HTTPS or localhost). Browsers without the API keep the standard page and links.
+
+Product information comes from the rendered cards; navigation comes from links marked with `data-agent-destination`. Logout is intentionally excluded from agent navigation. No checkout, account data, prices, or availability are invented: this repository only contains a homepage, and linked routes still require their existing hosting implementation. Opening the ordering link does not place an order.
+
+Tool inputs are validated at execution time. Navigation accepts known IDs rather than arbitrary URLs. Registration failures do not break the page, and registrations are released on page exit and restored when returning from the back/forward cache.
